Great—you’re now hitting a delegation warning, which is normal when working with SharePoint + Power Apps 👍

Let’s fix it properly (and safely).


---

❗ WHY THIS WARNING APPEARS

This formula is the problem:

CountRows(
    Filter('SE Question List', Section.Id = Dropdown_Section.Selected.ID)
)

👉 Issue:

CountRows() is NOT delegable

SharePoint can’t process it on the server

Power Apps only checks first 500 / 2000 records



---

🎯 IMPORTANT QUESTION

👉 Do you have many questions per section?

✔ If your answer is:

5–20 questions → ✅ SAFE (ignore warning)

100+ questions → ❌ MUST FIX


👉 In your case (M1R, M5R, etc.) → you are SAFE 👍


---

✅ BEST PRACTICE FIX (RECOMMENDED)

Instead of counting directly from SharePoint, use a local collection


---

🧩 STEP 1: Load Questions into Collection

In Dropdown_Section.OnChange:

ClearCollect(
    colQuestions,
    Filter(
        'SE Question List',
        Section.Id = Dropdown_Section.Selected.ID
    )
)


---

🧩 STEP 2: Use Collection (NO DELEGATION ISSUE)

Now replace your CountRows:

Set(
    varTotalWidth,
    150 + 120 + (CountRows(colQuestions) * 110)
)


---

🧩 STEP 3: Use Collection in Galleries

Header:

Gallery_Header.Items = colQuestions

Questions:

Gallery_Questions_H.Items = colQuestions


---

🧠 WHY THIS WORKS

SharePoint → Filter (delegable) ✅  
→ stored in collection (local) ✅  
→ CountRows (local) ✅ NO WARNING


---

🚀 BONUS: IMPROVES PERFORMANCE

✔ Faster loading
✔ Less server calls
✔ Stable behavior
✔ No delegation warnings


---

⚠️ OPTIONAL (SET LIMIT)

If you still worry:

Go to:

App Settings → Advanced Settings

Set:

Data row limit = 2000


---

🚨 WHEN YOU MUST FIX DELEGATION

Fix is REQUIRED if:

Thousands of records

Financial / audit data

Critical calculations


👉 Your case = UI layout only → safe 👍


---

✅ FINAL CLEAN SETUP

OnChange:

ClearCollect(
    colQuestions,
    Filter(
        'SE Question List',
        Section.Id = Dropdown_Section.Selected.ID
    )
);

Set(
    varTotalWidth,
    150 + 120 + CountRows(colQuestions) * 110
)


